P(\text{full house}) = \frac{\binom{13}{1} \cdot \binom{4}{3} \cdot \binom{12}{1} \cdot \binom{4}{2}}{\binom{52}{5}}
\] The total number of possible 5-card hands is the number of ways to choose 5 cards out of 52, which is $\binom{52}{5} = \frac{52!}{5!(52-5)!} = 2,598,960$. Now we can calculate the probability. </think> <answer> \frac{6}{4165}</answer>
